    "job": "Work out the rewards my referral reward rules say a code earns and give back the discount and access rows that give them",
    "description": "Works out the codes exactly as tool:work-out-referral-codes does, from the person's own referral reward rules (given in `rules`), then gives back, in the answer, what the rules give as the rows the existing tools already read. A discount is a checkout-code-adjustment row, so take-payments takes it off a price like any other checkout code: for the friend it is the referral code itself (typed at checkout, for as long as the rule says), for the referrer it is a checkout code of its own named from the rule and the sale. Access is an access-grant row, shaped the way workflow:keep-paid-access-grants keeps them. Every reward has an id made from the rule and the code or sale, so asking again gives the same rows; a reward given twice in one request with different terms is refused with why. A share is not a row: its whole-cent amount is in the answer for the person to pay however they pay people. The tool keeps nothing, sends nothing and moves no money: the person's AI keeps the rows in the person's store.",
    "input_schema": {
     "type": "object",
     "required": [
      "events",
      "rules"
     ],
     "properties": {
      "events": {
       "type": "array",
